  # ha-li-plugins
  
  Claude Code and Codex plugins for everyday git work.
  
  ## Install in Claude Code
  
  ```
  /plugin marketplace add ha-li/dstack
  /plugin install <plugin-name>@ha-li-plugins
  ```
  
  ## Install in Codex

  ```sh
  codex plugin marketplace add ha-li/dstack
  codex plugin add <plugin-name>@ha-li-plugins
  ```

  To use a local checkout instead, run this from the repository root:

  ```sh
  codex plugin marketplace add .
  ```

  The Codex catalog is `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json`. It references the
  existing Claude-compatible plugins; both catalogs use the same plugin folders.
  See [OpenAI's marketplace format documentation](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/plugin-management#supported-formats).

  ## Plugins
  
  | Plugin | What it does |
  |---|---|
  | `git-init-repo` | Connects a repo to a new remote and does the first push safely. Blocks force pushes. |
  | `pr-commit-plugin` | Writes commit messages, and checks staged files for secrets first. |
  | `dumbass` | Rewrites Claude's last answer in plain language. | 
  
